100788,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cpaK0","user":{"login":"psychicteeth","id":5365436,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNjU0MzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5365436?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/psychicteeth","html_url":"https://github.com/psychicteeth","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/psychicteeth/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/psychicteeth/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/psychicteeth/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/psychicteeth/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/psychicteeth/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/psychicteeth/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/psychicteeth/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/psychicteeth/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/psychicteeth/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-31T19:05:21Z","updated_at":"2025-01-31T19:05:21Z","body":"Thanks for the fast response. I've uploaded a project with the example scene in it and edited the original post.\n\nI see what you mean about the motion value being large, in that in physics situations you'd normally expect things to be moving much shorter distances between physics ticks. If this is the wrong function to be calling when doing ad-hoc sweeps, I'd be interested in hearing which part of the API is designed to help do this. Ray casts are not a universal solution for one-off collision checks. Every engine I've used has a way to sweep shapes and get collision data back. I haven't even addressed getting data back (colliders, normals etc) in this example, but it's not relevant to the issue as it's clear to me that the returned data isn't correct.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2628100788/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2628106506","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102254#issuecomment-2628106506","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102254","id":2628106506,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cpbkK","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-31T19:09:10Z","updated_at":"2025-01-31T19:09:10Z","body":"I'm not sure if this is a bug or not, it might depend on coordinate systems relative to different positions, unsure about the specifics, the physics experts would have to give their opinion\n\nIt could be due to recovery of the intersection, finding the closest \"safe\" position of the collision for example, might be good to test with different shapes to see how it behaves","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com